//! Runtime support for Rust code generated by `zant-tsx` from `.tsx`
//! components: the API the TSX backend (WP-5.3 … WP-5.6) emits calls to.
//!
//! Port of the 13 `src/tsx*.zig` runtime files (WP-5.7). Hand-written Rust
//! code rarely needs this module; it exists so generated code is small,
//! readable and independent of the internal framework modules:
//!
//! | Module | Zig source | What generated code calls |
//! |---|---|---|
//! | [`strings`] | `tsx_strings.zig` | JS string methods (`slice`, `split`, `replace`, …) |
//! | [`builtins`] / [`builtins_format`] | `tsx_builtins*.zig` | `Math.*`, `Number/parseInt/parseFloat`, `String(x)`, `toFixed` |
//! | [`timers`] | `tsx_timers.zig` | `setTimeout` / `setInterval` / `requestAnimationFrame` |
//! | [`platform`] | `tsx_platform.zig` | `clipboard`, `app`, `mainWindow`, `keyLabel`, `wakeAfter` |
//! | [`desktop`] | `tsx_desktop.zig` | `useTray` / `useHotkey` |
//! | [`app`] | `tsx_app.zig` | the shell around the root `ui::App`, `run`, `KeyEvent`, the theme |
//! | [`window`] | `tsx_window.zig` | `createWindow(Component)` |
//! | [`hooks`] | `tsx_hooks.zig` | `useMemo` / `useEffect` / `useRef` |
//! | [`text`] | `tsx_text.zig` | nested `<Text>` spans and inline `<Link>`s |
//! | [`native`] | `tsx_native.zig` | native module registry (WP-5.8) |
//!
//! Types used by the type mapping of `docs/rust-port/tsx-codegen.md` §2:
//!
//! - `string` → [`zant::Str`](crate::Str) (string literals are `Static`,
//!   runtime strings are `Str::copy(..)`),
//! - `T[]` → [`List<T>`] (`Rc<Vec<T>>` with copy-on-write mutation),
//! - `T | null` → `Option<T>`,
//! - `number` → `f64` / the context's integer type,
//! - `any` → [`Any`],
//! - `Uint8Array` → [`Bytes`].
//!
//! Parts of the Zig runtime that Rust does not need are **not** ported
//! (`docs/rust-port/tsx-codegen.md` §3 / plan.md M5):
//!
//! - `tsx.State(T)`, `tsx.String`, `tsx.deepCopy`: TS state maps to plain
//!   `Clone` fields (`Str`, [`List`], derived structs), `tsx.String` to
//!   [`crate::Str`]; the frame arena does not exist.
//! - `tsx.capture`, `tsx.concat`, `tsx.alloc`, `tsx.fmt`: closures capture
//!   values, `Vec`/`format!` replace the frame allocation and the Zig format
//!   pattern (float fields use [`builtins::string`] to get JS's spelling).
//! - `tsx.deinitFields`: `Drop` replaces the field walk; local state lives in
//!   `Rc<RefCell<T>>` slots.
//! - `tsx.Callback(fn (..) void)`: Rust closures are [`hooks::Callback`]
//!   (`Rc<dyn Fn(..)>`).
//!
//! Types and helpers below are re-exported at the module root so generated
//! code spells them `tsx::…` like the Zig compiler's `tsx.…`.
#![forbid(unsafe_code)]

#[forbid(unsafe_code)]
pub mod any;
#[forbid(unsafe_code)]
pub mod app;
#[forbid(unsafe_code)]
